0.1736.513Without acquiescing to the Office's interpretation of Petroff in view of Claim 1, Applicant respectfully asserts that Petroff only teaches that the AV 102 stops at the stop line 305. However, Petroff is silent in regards to "a maximum velocity" of the vehicle "at which the vehicle can stop immediately before the intersection" in regard to a "right of way". Merely requiring the AV 102 to stop at the stop line 305 does not teach "a maximum velocity", and more specifically "setting a maximum velocity, as an upper limit velocity of the vehicle, at which the vehicle can stop immediately before the intersection", as recited in amended Claim 1.
